        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet, bdbro: Reject revisited overflow pages\n\nEnforcing overflow data lengths stops a chain whose pages carry data,\nbut overflow pages that carry no data never advance the accumulated\nlength, so a chain that cycles through empty overflow pages loops\nforever. Any number of records can also point at the same chain, which\nis then read and stored once per record.\n\nIn a valid database each overflow page belongs to one record, so keep\ntrack of the overflow pages visited across the whole tree and reject\none that is seen again.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Shuvam Pandey",
        "email": "shuvampandey1@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-06T14:49:22Z"
